      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T16:02:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. New fds just use the smallest available fd number, so it\u0027s pretty easy to guess. My point is, you\u0027re not really supposed to be able to call `i_size_write` on arbitrary inodes, but this driver now lets you do exactly that. Maybe some other driver uses the inode size for bounds check, and combined with this you can now bypass bounds check in other driver?",
      "parentUuid": "18bb281c_b3197173",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
